1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:06,196
Meet Axin: smarter bus journeys in Baku, with useful insights for transport

2
00:00:06,196 --> 00:00:06,700
operators.

3
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:12,654
First, search your destination. Use your location with permission, or choose another

4
00:00:12,654 --> 00:00:17,700
starting point. Axin checks nearby boarding stops, not just the closest.

5
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:24,450
Compare up to three options, prioritizing fewer transfers. Tags highlight speed, crowding,

6
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:29,700
and fewer boardings. Trips under one kilometre become walking routes.

7
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:35,905
The map highlights your journey, boarding stops, transfers, and destination. Switch layers,

8
00:00:35,905 --> 00:00:40,700
zoom, or find your location. Simulated buses follow route geometry.

9
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:46,880
Arrival time combines walking, waiting, riding, and transfers. The simulated fleet targets

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,700
six-minute intervals. Times are estimates, without live traffic.

11
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:56,607
Report low, medium, or high crowding. Reports are saved. Optional GPS participation

12
00:00:56,607 --> 00:01:00,700
requires consent and estimates participating devices, not every passenger.

13
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:07,480
Operators monitor routes, fleet activity, and crowding. Ten minutes of qualifying high

14
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:11,700
crowding triggers an alert recommending an additional bus.

15
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:17,019
Select a line, complete trajectory, and eligible reserve bus. The server validates

16
00:01:17,019 --> 00:01:21,888
and records the assignment. The bus starts in simulation; no physical bus

17
00:01:21,888 --> 00:01:22,700
is dispatched.

18
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:29,700
Axin connects official open data and simulated movement for better-informed journeys.
